 from the checkout, merging these changes into any customized view first.
+
+# Comment Escape browser check
+
+Requires Cargo, Chrome and `playwright-cli`. Build from the checkout and start a
+fresh throwaway daemon:
+
+```sh
+cargo build --locked --target-dir /tmp/jelly-escape-target
+/tmp/jelly-escape-target/debug/jelly serve --port 17883 --home /tmp/jelly-escape-home
+```
+
+In another terminal, create the map fixture and run the browser check from a
+scratch directory:
+
+```sh
+/tmp/jelly-escape-target/debug/jelly --url http://127.0.0.1:17883 new escape:map --from skill/recipes/map
+playwright-cli -s=escape open http://127.0.0.1:17883/
+playwright-cli -s=escape run-code --filename=/path/to/jelly/tests/comment-escape.js
+playwright-cli -s=escape close
+```
+
+The check walks the map trace in a standalone jelly and the embedded full view.
+It verifies that Escape ends commenting while preserving the current step, that
+the next Escape dismisses the trace, and that Escape still cancels the comment
+editor. It fails on the pre-fix runtime.
